# `gcloud builds submit` does NOT read .dockerignore -- it reads this file.
# Without it the first submit uploaded 634 MiB across 20,297 files, almost all
# of it the macOS arm64 .venv, which the image cannot use and the build does
# not need.
#
# Kept deliberately close to .dockerignore. The two files serve different
# stages -- this one bounds what is uploaded, that one bounds what is copied
# into a layer -- so they are not interchangeable, but a path that must not
# reach a layer generally has no business being uploaded either.

.venv/
venv/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.chroma/
.workspaces/
checkpoints.db*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

tests/
probes/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.lock-report.json

.DS_Store
